 ### Hook Types
 
-- `pre-install`: Before templates rendered
-- `post-install`: After all resources loaded
-- `pre-delete`: Before any resources deleted
-- `post-delete`: After all resources deleted
-- `pre-upgrade`: Before upgrade
-- `post-upgrade`: After upgrade
-- `pre-rollback`: Before rollback
-- `post-rollback`: After rollback
-- `test`: Run with `helm test`
+- `pre-install`: After template rendering and before ordinary release resources are created; CRDs from `crds/` are handled earlier.
+- `post-install`: After ordinary release resources are loaded; `--wait` delays this hook until they are ready.
+- `pre-delete`: Before release resources are deleted.
+- `post-delete`: After release resources are deleted.
+- `pre-upgrade`: After rendering and before release resources are updated.
+- `post-upgrade`: After release resources are updated.
+- `pre-rollback`: After rendering and before release resources are rolled back.
+- `post-rollback`: After release resources are rolled back.
+- `test`: Run with an explicitly authorized `helm test`.
+
+A pre-install or pre-upgrade hook cannot produce values needed by that same render.
+Use migration hooks only under an explicit project contract for bounded execution,
+idempotency, concurrency, schema compatibility, failure recovery and cleanup.
+See the [Helm hook lifecycle](https://docs.helm.sh/docs/topics/charts_hooks/).
 
 ### Hook Weight
 
-Controls hook execution order (-5 to 5, lower runs first)
+`helm.sh/hook-weight` is a signed integer represented as a quoted string, with
+`"0"` as the default. Helm sorts weights in ascending order (negative to positive),
+then resource kind and name for ties. There is no documented `-5` to `5` range;
+check ordering details against the selected Helm version and avoid relying on
+incidental ordering between equal-weight hooks.
 
 ### Hook Deletion Policies
 
